 "notes": "The Hilma Hooker (71.8 m x 11 m) on her starboard side in the sand channel between the inner and outer reef, 18 m at the top of the hull and 30-34 m at the sand, marked by three yellow moorings (bow, stern and one on the reef); shore entry at the yellow stones south end of the car park (Wikipedia, bonaire.com, chronic-wanderlust.com, scubadiving.com). The wreck's position is from the Wikidata point, on the sand channel; she is drawn parallel to the channel (147 deg), with the bow south and the propeller north as most sources say, though bonaire.com puts the bow north-west. Outer-reef width and the reef mooring spot are assumptions. Coastline and dive-site markers © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Positions are approximate.",
